title: K-Path Selection
keyword: BZ SPECIAL
manual: structure/#c2-bz
cite: hinuma_2017

Chooses the path through k-points for a band structure calculation and writes it in the
format of an electronic structure code. Tools > Structure Analysis > K-Path Selection
switches the view to reciprocal space and opens the editor of its k-path object, making one
if there is none (Draw > K-Path adds more). A new path is the one suggested for the crystal
by Hinuma et al., which the BZ SPECIAL keyword prints with the special k-points. The path is
drawn in the view as arrows from each point to the next. Only crystals have k-paths.

# Options

- "Name" and "Show": the name of the object and whether it is drawn.
- "Path": a table of the points, in order, with the label, the coordinates in the reciprocal
  basis of this cell (hkl) and the distance to the origin. The red cross removes a point;
  "Break" makes the path jump to that point, with no segment from the previous one; the
  label can be edited (HPKOT notation, e.g. GAMMA, X_1). The point of the row under the
  mouse is highlighted in the view. Click a row to select it, and again to unselect it.
- "Add Point": click a special k-point or a reciprocal lattice point in the view to add it
  after the selected point, or at the end if none is selected.
- "Move Up" and "Move Down" change the place of the selected point in the path. "Reset to
  Suggested Path" replaces the path with the suggested one.
- "Style": the "Radius (1/Å)" and "Color" of the arrows, the spheres at the "Points" with
  their "Point radius (1/Å)", and the "Labels" of the points with their size, color and
  offset.

# Results

The "Export" section writes the path in the chosen "Format": a text table of labels and
coordinates, the K_POINTS crystal_b card of Quantum ESPRESSO, or a VASP KPOINTS file in line
mode, the last two with the given number of "Points per segment". "Write to Output" sends it
to the Output console and "Write to File..." to a file. The coordinates are in the reciprocal
basis of the cell of this system, which must be the one of the calculation. "Reset" restores
the defaults and replaces the path with the suggested one.
